---@field remoteLoginPortPublicAccess? azure.machinelearningservices.AmlComputePropertiesRemoteLoginPortPublicAccess State of the public SSH port. Possible values are: Disabled - Indicates that the public ssh port is closed on all nodes of the cluster. Enabled - Indicates that the public ssh port is open on all nodes of the cluster. NotSpecified - Indicates that the public ssh port is closed on all nodes of the cluster if VNet is defined, else is open all public nodes. It can be default only during cluster creation time, after creation it will be either enabled or disabled.
---@field allocationState? azure.machinelearningservices.AllocationState Allocation state of the compute. Possible values are: steady - Indicates that the compute is not resizing. There are no changes to the number of compute nodes in the compute in progress. A compute enters this state when it is created and when no operations are being performed on the compute to change the number of compute nodes. resizing - Indicates that the compute is resizing; that is, compute nodes are being added to or removed from the compute.
---@field allocationStateTransitionTime? string The time at which the compute entered its current allocation state.
---@field errors? azure.machinelearningservices.AmlComputePropertiesErrorsList|distilled.Null Collection of errors encountered by various compute nodes during node setup.
---@field currentNodeCount? number|distilled.Null The number of compute nodes currently assigned to the compute.
---@field targetNodeCount? number|distilled.Null The target number of compute nodes for the compute. If the allocationState is resizing, this property denotes the target node count for the ongoing resize operation. If the allocationState is steady, this property denotes the target node count for the previous resize operation.
---@field nodeStateCounts? azure.machinelearningservices.NodeStateCounts|distilled.Null Counts of various node states on the compute.
---@field enableNodePublicIp? boolean|distilled.Null Enable or disable node public IP address provisioning. Possible values are: Possible values are: true - Indicates that the compute nodes will have public IPs provisioned. false - Indicates that the compute nodes will have a private endpoint and no public IPs.
