---Distribution expressions to sweep over values of model settings.
---<example>
---Some examples are:
---```
---ModelName = "choice('seresnext', 'resnest50')";
---LearningRate = "uniform(0.001, 0.01)";
---LayersToFreeze = "choice(0, 2)";
---```</example>
---For more details on how to compose distribution expressions please check the documentation:
---https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-tune-hyperparameters
---For more information on the available settings please visit the official documentation:
---https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-auto-train-image-models.
---@class azure.machinelearningservices.ImageModelDistributionSettingsClassification
---@field amsGradient? string|distilled.Null Enable AMSGrad when optimizer is 'adam' or 'adamw'.
---@field augmentations? string|distilled.Null Settings for using Augmentations.
---@field beta1? string|distilled.Null Value of 'beta1' when optimizer is 'adam' or 'adamw'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field beta2? string|distilled.Null Value of 'beta2' when optimizer is 'adam' or 'adamw'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field distributed? string|distilled.Null Whether to use distributer training.
---@field earlyStopping? string|distilled.Null Enable early stopping logic during training.
---@field earlyStoppingDelay? string|distilled.Null Minimum number of epochs or validation evaluations to wait before primary metric improvement is tracked for early stopping. Must be a positive integer.
---@field earlyStoppingPatience? string|distilled.Null Minimum number of epochs or validation evaluations with no primary metric improvement before the run is stopped. Must be a positive integer.
---@field enableOnnxNormalization? string|distilled.Null Enable normalization when exporting ONNX model.
---@field evaluationFrequency? string|distilled.Null Frequency to evaluate validation dataset to get metric scores. Must be a positive integer.
---@field gradientAccumulationStep? string|distilled.Null Gradient accumulation means running a configured number of "GradAccumulationStep" steps without updating the model weights while accumulating the gradients of those steps, and then using the accumulated gradients to compute the weight updates. Must be a positive integer.
---@field layersToFreeze? string|distilled.Null Number of layers to freeze for the model. Must be a positive integer. For instance, passing 2 as value for 'seresnext' means freezing layer0 and layer1. For a full list of models supported and details on layer freeze, please see: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-auto-train-image-models.
---@field learningRate? string|distilled.Null Initial learning rate. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field learningRateScheduler? string|distilled.Null Type of learning rate scheduler. Must be 'warmup_cosine' or 'step'.
---@field modelName? string|distilled.Null Name of the model to use for training. For more information on the available models please visit the official documentation: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-auto-train-image-models.
---@field momentum? string|distilled.Null Value of momentum when optimizer is 'sgd'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field nesterov? string|distilled.Null Enable nesterov when optimizer is 'sgd'.
---@field numberOfEpochs? string|distilled.Null Number of training epochs. Must be a positive integer.
---@field numberOfWorkers? string|distilled.Null Number of data loader workers. Must be a non-negative integer.
---@field optimizer? string|distilled.Null Type of optimizer. Must be either 'sgd', 'adam', or 'adamw'.
---@field randomSeed? string|distilled.Null Random seed to be used when using deterministic training.
---@field stepLRGamma? string|distilled.Null Value of gamma when learning rate scheduler is 'step'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field stepLRStepSize? string|distilled.Null Value of step size when learning rate scheduler is 'step'. Must be a positive integer.
---@field trainingBatchSize? string|distilled.Null Training batch size. Must be a positive integer.
---@field validationBatchSize? string|distilled.Null Validation batch size. Must be a positive integer.
---@field warmupCosineLRCycles? string|distilled.Null Value of cosine cycle when learning rate scheduler is 'warmup_cosine'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field warmupCosineLRWarmupEpochs? string|distilled.Null Value of warmup epochs when learning rate scheduler is 'warmup_cosine'. Must be a positive integer.
---@field weightDecay? string|distilled.Null Value of weight decay when optimizer is 'sgd', 'adam', or 'adamw'. Must be a float in the range[0, 1].
---@field trainingCropSize? string|distilled.Null Image crop size that is input to the neural network for the training dataset. Must be a positive integer.
---@field validationCropSize? string|distilled.Null Image crop size that is input to the neural network for the validation dataset. Must be a positive integer.
---@field validationResizeSize? string|distilled.Null Image size to which to resize before cropping for validation dataset. Must be a positive integer.
---@field weightedLoss? string|distilled.Null Weighted loss. The accepted values are 0 for no weighted loss. 1 for weighted loss with sqrt.(class_weights). 2 for weighted loss with class_weights. Must be 0 or 1 or 2.

