---@field checkpointModel? azure.machinelearningservices.MLFlowModelJobInput|distilled.Null The pretrained checkpoint model for incremental training.
---@field checkpointRunId? string|distilled.Null The id of a previous run that has a pretrained checkpoint for incremental training.
---@field distributed? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to use distributed training.
---@field earlyStopping? boolean|distilled.Null Enable early stopping logic during training.
---@field earlyStoppingDelay? number|distilled.Null Minimum number of epochs or validation evaluations to wait before primary metric improvement is tracked for early stopping. Must be a positive integer.
---@field earlyStoppingPatience? number|distilled.Null Minimum number of epochs or validation evaluations with no primary metric improvement before the run is stopped. Must be a positive integer.
---@field enableOnnxNormalization? boolean|distilled.Null Enable normalization when exporting ONNX model.
---@field evaluationFrequency? number|distilled.Null Frequency to evaluate validation dataset to get metric scores. Must be a positive integer.
---@field gradientAccumulationStep? number|distilled.Null Gradient accumulation means running a configured number of "GradAccumulationStep" steps without updating the model weights while accumulating the gradients of those steps, and then using the accumulated gradients to compute the weight updates. Must be a positive integer.
---@field layersToFreeze? number|distilled.Null Number of layers to freeze for the model. Must be a positive integer. For instance, passing 2 as value for 'seresnext' means freezing layer0 and layer1. For a full list of models supported and details on layer freeze, please see: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-auto-train-image-models.
---@field learningRate? number|distilled.Null Initial learning rate. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field learningRateScheduler? azure.machinelearningservices.ImageModelSettingsObjectDetectionLearningRateScheduler|string Learning rate scheduler enum.
---@field modelName? string|distilled.Null Name of the model to use for training. For more information on the available models please visit the official documentation: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/how-to-auto-train-image-models.
---@field momentum? number|distilled.Null Value of momentum when optimizer is 'sgd'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field nesterov? boolean|distilled.Null Enable nesterov when optimizer is 'sgd'.
---@field numberOfEpochs? number|distilled.Null Number of training epochs. Must be a positive integer.
---@field numberOfWorkers? number|distilled.Null Number of data loader workers. Must be a non-negative integer.
---@field optimizer? azure.machinelearningservices.ImageModelSettingsObjectDetectionOptimizer|string Stochastic optimizer for image models.
---@field randomSeed? number|distilled.Null Random seed to be used when using deterministic training.
---@field stepLRGamma? number|distilled.Null Value of gamma when learning rate scheduler is 'step'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field stepLRStepSize? number|distilled.Null Value of step size when learning rate scheduler is 'step'. Must be a positive integer.
---@field trainingBatchSize? number|distilled.Null Training batch size. Must be a positive integer.
---@field validationBatchSize? number|distilled.Null Validation batch size. Must be a positive integer.
---@field warmupCosineLRCycles? number|distilled.Null Value of cosine cycle when learning rate scheduler is 'warmup_cosine'. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field warmupCosineLRWarmupEpochs? number|distilled.Null Value of warmup epochs when learning rate scheduler is 'warmup_cosine'. Must be a positive integer.
---@field weightDecay? number|distilled.Null Value of weight decay when optimizer is 'sgd', 'adam', or 'adamw'. Must be a float in the range[0, 1].
---@field boxDetectionsPerImage? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of detections per image, for all classes. Must be a positive integer. Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field boxScoreThreshold? number|distilled.Null During inference, only return proposals with a classification score greater than BoxScoreThreshold. Must be a float in the range[0, 1].
---@field imageSize? number|distilled.Null Image size for train and validation. Must be a positive integer. Note: The training run may get into CUDA OOM if the size is too big. Note: This settings is only supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field maxSize? number|distilled.Null Maximum size of the image to be rescaled before feeding it to the backbone. Must be a positive integer. Note: training run may get into CUDA OOM if the size is too big. Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field minSize? number|distilled.Null Minimum size of the image to be rescaled before feeding it to the backbone. Must be a positive integer. Note: training run may get into CUDA OOM if the size is too big. Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field modelSize? azure.machinelearningservices.ImageModelSettingsObjectDetectionModelSize|string Image model size.
---@field multiScale? boolean|distilled.Null Enable multi-scale image by varying image size by +/- 50%. Note: training run may get into CUDA OOM if no sufficient GPU memory. Note: This settings is only supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field nmsIouThreshold? number|distilled.Null IOU threshold used during inference in NMS post processing. Must be a float in the range [0, 1].
---@field tileGridSize? string|distilled.Null The grid size to use for tiling each image. Note: TileGridSize must not be None to enable small object detection logic. A string containing two integers in mxn format. Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field tileOverlapRatio? number|distilled.Null Overlap ratio between adjacent tiles in each dimension. Must be float in the range [0, 1). Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field tilePredictionsNmsThreshold? number|distilled.Null The IOU threshold to use to perform NMS while merging predictions from tiles and image. Used in validation/ inference. Must be float in the range [0, 1]. Note: This settings is not supported for the 'yolov5' algorithm.
---@field validationIouThreshold? number|distilled.Null IOU threshold to use when computing validation metric. Must be float in the range [0, 1].
